                -- Update dropdown's displayed value (WindUI might not have a direct setter, but we can try to change internal state)
                -- Since WindUI dropdown doesn't expose a SetValue method easily, we'll just notify and let user manually select.
                -- However we can try to simulate: the dropdown's callback will be triggered when user selects, but we can manually set the selectedPlot variable.
                WindUI:Notify({
                    Title = "Plot Found!",
                    Content = "Your plot is #" .. myPlot .. ". Please select it from the dropdown.",
                    Duration = 4,
                    Icon = "check-circle"
                })
                -- Optionally, we could try to update the dropdown's displayed text, but it's fine.
            else
                WindUI:Notify({
                    Title = "Not Found",
